// A generic prelude struct named in a signature and never built, whose own field
// names another instance.
//
// The reference emits `Slot_i32_bool` before the `HashMap_i32_bool` whose
// `slots` field points at it; the port emitted them the other way round. The
// resolution site already had the rule - fields before self, with the comment
// naming the measurement it was written from - so the defect was a BYPASS of it,
// not its absence.
//
// The bypass: signature collection is the FIRST pass to resolve a type, and it
// ran with no skeleton in scope. An instance minted there registers no fields,
// so the nested instances its fields name are not minted with it, and the
// container reaches the aggregate list first. A BUILT HashMap agreed throughout,
// which is what located the pass.
fn takes(h: *const HashMap<int, bool>) { println(1); }

fn main() { println(1); }
